---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import EmailCTA from '../components/EmailCTA.astro';
import TipJar from '../components/TipJar.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About — Spiked Adrenaline"
  description="Spiked Adrenaline is a Montana-based backcountry field-testing outfit. Gear tested on real hunts and real miles — anonymous by design."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who we are</p>
    <h1>The site is the tester.</h1>
    <p>
      Spiked Adrenaline is a Montana-based backcountry field-testing outfit. Gear gets tested
      on real hunts and real backpacking miles — not on a porch, and not from a press release.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're anonymous by design. In hunting culture, protecting spots — and identities — is
      respected, not suspicious. You won't find names, faces, or trailheads here. You'll find
      nights out, load weights, temperature swings, and honest calls on what held up and what failed.
    </p>
    <h2>How we test</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Real miles.</strong> Every review states nights out, conditions, and load.</li>
      <li><strong>Failures included.</strong> What broke and what annoyed us goes in the review. That's the trust engine.</li>
      <li><strong>Who it's for — and who it's not for.</strong> Every verdict says both, explicitly.</li>
      <li><strong>Willing to say "skip it."</strong> No hype words unless the data earns them.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How this site makes money</h2>
    <p>
      Some links are affiliate links: buy through them and we may earn a commission at no extra
      cost to you. That funds more gear and more nights out. It never changes a verdict — a review
      that can't say "skip it" isn't worth reading.
    </p>
    <TipJar />
    <EmailCTA />
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  section { margin-top: 3rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 6vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; }
  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
</style>
